+## Symbolic links
+
+Symbolic links in `.zip` and `.sqfs` archives are skipped unless
+`-l`/`--links` is in use, in which case they are shown as files with
+the `.rclonelink` suffix whose contents are the link target, just as
+for the [local backend](/local/#symlinks--junction-points).
+
+```
+$ rclone lsl --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip
+        5 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/file.txt
+        8 2026-09-28 14:16:59.000000000 src/link.txt.rclonelink
+$ rclone copy --links :archive:/tmp/test.zip /tmp/out
+$ ls -l /tmp/out/src/link.txt
+lrwxr-xr-x 1 user user 8 Sep 28 14:16 /tmp/out/src/link.txt -> file.txt
+```
+
+A regular file whose name happens to end in `.rclonelink` is still
+read as a regular file.
+
 ## Hashes
 
 Which hash is supported depends on the archive type. Zip files use
